title: $:/plugins/nikorion/palette/language/en-GB/readme
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

nikorion's colour palette, based on TiddlyWiki's default (Vanilla) palette. It is selected by default: the plugin ships `$:/palette` pointing to it.

! What it provides

* `$:/palettes/nikorion`: the palette, a copy of the default one to adjust colour by colour (//Control Panel → Appearance → Palette//, or edit the tiddler).
* `$:/palette`: selects it.

! Use with the Theme plugin

Beyond the standard keys, the palette carries the colours of the [[Theme|https://github.com/nikorion/TW-Theme]] plugin (`nk-site-title`, `nk-hljs-*`, `nk-info-*`…). The theme reads every key as a CSS variable `--tpc-<key>`, so it hard-codes no colour: change a value here and the theme follows. Other themes use the standard keys through `<<colour name>>`.

! Requirements

TiddlyWiki >= 5.3.5.
